WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:04.550
Zoe T: My name's Zoe.

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:11.435
I am mum to Phillip, who is nearly
22 and Louie who is 18 next week.

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:15.260
Phillip has a diagnosis of
autism and Louie doesn't.

00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:16.340
I am a widow.

00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:21.320
I live in Oldham and I run Bright Future
School for children with autism, which is

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:26.955
in Greenfield, which is about 10 minutes
drive from here, which I set up in 2010

00:00:26.955 --> 00:00:33.375
with my late husband because we couldn't
find anywhere - well, I say we, the local

00:00:33.375 --> 00:00:37.905
authority couldn't find anywhere, a school
that was suitable to meet Phillip's needs.

00:00:37.965 --> 00:00:44.445
And at that point we had just
starting taking part in an autism

00:00:44.445 --> 00:00:47.535
intervention called Relationship
Development Intervention, which made

00:00:47.535 --> 00:00:51.105
a massive difference to our lives
and our ability to understand Phillip

00:00:51.105 --> 00:00:54.105
and his ability to engage with us.

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:59.460
Because that worked on the core
difficulties at the heart of autism

00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:05.640
and because the autism was, as far as
we could see, the main thing that was

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:12.440
the obstacle for Phillip to engage in
education and with the wider world.

00:01:13.785 --> 00:01:17.445
We wanted a school placement
that would embed those sorts of

00:01:17.445 --> 00:01:19.725
principles into the school day.

00:01:19.995 --> 00:01:23.505
We couldn't find one, so we ended
up setting up our own school.

